Subject: [PATCH 10/12] =?UTF-8?q?kcm=5Fkwinrules:=20labelled=20actions,=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?row=20opens=20the=20editor,=20"=E2=80=A6"=20menu,=20empty=20sta?=
 =?UTF-8?q?tes=20with=20an=20action?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List with the rule editor as the existing sub-page (docs/page-design.md 1, 4). Rule storage (kwinrulesrc), policies,
properties, the uuid/whole-app launch arguments and the window-info D-Bus calls are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Toolbar: "Add New…" -> "Add Rule…", "Import…" -> "Import Rules…", "Export…" -> "Export Rules…" (names say what is added).
  Old wording added to the page aliases in ia/layout.json ("special window settings", "add new rule").
- Rule row: clicking the row opens the editor (was only the Edit button); two inline icon actions (Edit, Delete) and a "…"
  menu with Duplicate (was three icon buttons). Buttons are flat, have tooltips and Accessible.name.
- Empty list: placeholder "No window rules yet" with an "Add Rule…" button (was text that told to click a toolbar button).
- Editor: "Add Property..." -> "Add Property…", "Detect Window Properties" -> "Detect Window Properties…" (opens a picker or
  waits for a click), empty state gets an "Add Property…" button, the per-property remove button gets a tooltip and name
  ("Remove Property"; was an unnamed icon button).
- Markers and relabel table (inventory/relabel/kcm_kwinrules.tsv); markers also added on the weak rows (policy combo,
  value editors, add-property sheet, delay spin, export buttons, launch args) so --strict can prove them. --strict: 68 ok, 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-019, HIG-047 (empty state with action), HIG-058, HIG-066 (accessible names). Page-design 3, 4.

Speed: no blocking work found. The constructor only builds the 44 RuleItems (in memory), kwinrulesrc is read in load(),
getWindowInfo and the detect call are already async (kcmrules.cpp parseArguments, rulesmodel.cpp), and the editor is created
only by kcm.push when a rule is opened. Nothing changed there; the section/row count stays (4 sections: Window matching,
Size & Position, Arrangement & Access, Appearance & Fixes, left as the model names them).
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: QQC2.Menu.popup(item, x, y) and
icon "overflow-menu" in the delegate; the row onClicked sharing space with the borderless description TextField.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
